  "recreation_notes": [
    {
      "line_end": 125,
      "line_start": 1,
      "status": "candidate",
      "text": "____       _ _           ____\n|  _ \\ ___ | | | ___ _ __/ ___| __ _ _ __ ___   ___  ___\n| |_) / _ \\| | |/ _ \\ '__| |  _ / _` | '_ ` _ \\ / _ \\/ __|\n|  _ < (_) | | |  __/ |  | |_| | (_| | | | | | |  __/\\__ \\\n|_| \\_\\___/|_|_|\\___|_|   \\____|\\__,_|_| |_| |_|\\___||___/\n\n             W I L L I A M S   1 9 9 0\n\n       MrJ Definitive Edition 2.1 - VR Update\n\n Gameplay restoration, lighting, flashers, VR display,\n backglass GI, WILLIAMS lamps, and visual refinements.\n\n Skate or Die!\n************************************************************\nRelease 06/14/26\nMrJ Definitive Edition VR Update\n2.1.1 Updates\n\nDisplay & Compatibility\n-Corrected FlexDMD timing conflicts\n-Corrected FlexDMD ghosting reported by Pin2DMD users\n-Improved synchronization between FlexDMD and VR/FSS alpha-numeric displays\n-Corrected display update handling when multiple display systems are active\n-Improved compatibility across Desktop, Cabinet, VR and FSS modes\n\nScript Improvements\n-Optimized display timer processing\n-Reduced redundant display polling operations\n-Improved display initialization stability\n-Additional script cleanup and refinements\n************************************************************\nRelease 06/13/26\nMrJ Definitive Edition VR Update\n2.1 Updates\n\n-Added VR support and VR room enhancements\n-Added alpha-numeric scoring display [System 11]\n-Added illumination for backglass WILLIAMS progression\n-Added general illumination to backglass with GI on/off features\n-Added speaker grill illumination\n-Added VR test region\n-Added desktop arcade backdrop courtesy of Cliffy\n-Added FSS arcade backdrop environment\n-Adjusted Desktop POV for improved depth and aspect ratio\n-Adjusted FSS POV for improved depth and aspect ratio\n-Improved FSS presentation with integrated backglass environment\n\n-Corrected GI ON/OFF transitions for VR backglass elements\n-Corrected visibility handling for VR room assets\n-Improved support for Desktop, Cabinet, VR and FSS viewing modes\n\n-Additional lighting, display, and presentation refinements\n************************************************************\nRelease 06/11/26\nMrJ Definitive Edition\n2.0 Updates\n\nGameplay\n-Fixed upper lock behavior\n-Fixed Atomic Whip ball path\n-Fixed timing issues\n-Improved plunge options and skill shots\n-Reduced ramp rejects\n-Reduced magnet flip rejects\n-Fixed airball issue\n-Eliminated multiple stuck-ball locations\n-Added protection for game-breaking stuck scenarios\n\nLighting\n-Rebuilt GI to better match the real machine\n-Added missing GI locations\n-Corrected GI/LUT interaction\n-Fixed SPECIAL insert lighting\n-Improved insert illumination\n-Reduced excessive bloom\n\nVisuals\n-Adjusted cabinet POV\n-Restored missing magnet artwork\n-Added realistic magnet surface\n-Improved pop bumpers [Added all new pop bumpers and matching GI illumination]\n-Improved ramp transparency\n-Added missing decals\n-Fixed visibility issues under ramps\n-Modernized ball rendering\n\nAuthenticity\n-Verified Light66 and Light45 independently\n-Corrected flasher sequencing\n-Repositioned flashers to match the real machine\n-Matched GI placement to real-world references\n\nStability\n-Fixed script issues\n-Corrected GI collection problems\n-Removed legacy rendering warning\n-Eliminated multiple ball traps\n\n******************************************\nModified by drakkon, version 1.0\n\n-VR Room Added by Ext2k, 27th January 2025 thanks to Ahr1man for first attempt to convert it.\n\n******************************************\n\nModified by drakkon, version 1.0\n\n1.1 Updates:\n-Added FlexDMD, thanks to scutters for adding FlexDMD support\n  -Fixed kickback ball getting stuck on end of drop, was infrequent issue\n-Added TargetBouncer\n  -Added dynamic ball shadows\n-Added LUT selection\n\n1.0 Updates - Initial Release:\n-nFozzy physics\n-fleep mechanical sounds\n-minor visual updates (drop targets, plunger decal, \"the pit\" decal\n\n******************************************\n\nOriginal version created by javier1515, \"RollerGames (Williams 1990) 1.01a\"\n\n******************************************"
    },
